New Rock is a subdialect of the Rock language, a simple C-like language
compiling down to Pebble. New rock adds many extra featues, but it
mainly adds proper Pebble addressing support to the language to allow
all of the advanced concepts that can be expressed by Pebble AAE to also
be expressed by the Rock language. This does mean New Rock removed the
older Rock marker symbols, meaning code written in Rock will not compile
with a New Rock compiler.

The New Rock compiler can be found in the rockc/ folder relative to here
and can be compiled simply with

	cc -o rockc rockc/*.c

to generate one rockc binary. Running this without arguments should
tell you how to use it

rockpkg is a small package manager for the New Rock language, which can
be found in the rockpkg/ directory.
